Z||000009||rockcrawl||03-26-2001||05:00 PM||||$290.37 for GM or $200. for repros? I'd buy the GM ones. I've seen a few sets of repros (not Dougs) and they all had problems with the paint separating from the acrylic where the mounting tape was. Also, the edges were not rolled exactly like the originals, and they were slightly wavy. I understand Doug's windows don't have any of these problems, but I'd rather spend the extra $90 and be sure.<P>Also, if anyone is interested in making reproduction windows, let me know. I recently had a set of window bucks offered to me by a local guy who's getting out of Fieros. I have no idea what they look like or what's involved in making them, but the bucks are free.||||reg||1
Z||000010||RDosdorian||03-26-2001||05:09 PM||||The problem with the GM ones is that they are not being produced any longer.  There may be a few sets sitting with a dealer somewhere, but they are no longer available through GM.  This is per my inquiry with my local Chevy dealer about four months ago.||||reg||1
